  (text "CPU data pins CD0-CD7 carry the bank address while PHI2 is low.\nThe CPLD latches BA0-BA3 from CD0-CD3; the 74AHC245 is only enabled\n(BUF_OE low) while PHI2 is high, so the bank byte never reaches the\nsystem bus. RDY has a pull-up rather than a tie to +5V because WAI\ndrives it low. BE is held high. The CPU is the PLCC-44 W65C816S6PLG.\nJ1 brings out E (emulation mode) for debugging." (at 25.4 166.06 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 70a8b30e-8d09-4734-9cbd-54b02b6e01a2)
  )
)
